Every clinician should use an NSAID at a lowest-effective-dose during a shortest-needed-duration.
If a patient is an older-adult then every clinician should heed an NSAID-caution.
If a patient has a cardiovascular-comorbidity or has a chronic-renal-failure then every clinician should heed an NSAID-caution.
If a patient has a previous-gastrointestinal-bleeding then every clinician should heed an NSAID-caution.
